    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0367" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 867.00/44</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral W. S. Benson to
                        the Secretary of the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">M–5/G</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-29">29 December,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Grew</hi>: Replying to your letter of
                    the 28th instant<anchor n="6" xml:id="d196-f1"/> to which you attached a copy of
                    the telegram from the American Minister at Athens,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d196-f2"
                    /> stating as his opinion, that it would be desirable for the United States to
                    send an Admiral as High Commissioner at Constantinople; I beg to inform you that
                    this matter was taken up a fortnight ago with the Navy Department, and by that
                    Department was taken up with the Department of State.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d196-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have since been informed that the view of the Department of State is that it
                    will be unnecessary to send an officer of high rank to Constantinople at the
                    present time, but that a Flag Officer should be sent with a station-ship at
                    Salonica. In conformance with this policy the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nahma</hi> has been ordered to Salonica and Rear-Admiral M. L. Bristol has
                    been directed to proceed to that port and to hoist his flag on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nahma.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. S. Benson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
